DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzppuuzzzzllee is the classic fifteen puzzle: fifteen numbered
     tiles and one gap on a four-by-four board.  Slide the tiles
     until they read 1 to 15 in order.  It must be run under the
     zzvviieeww desktop and accepts the standard window _o_p_t_i_o_n_s of GUI
     applications; see zzvviieeww.

     A left click on any tile in the same row or column as the
     gap slides the whole run of tiles between it and the gap one
     place - so one click can move several tiles.  Clicks else-
     where are ignored.

     The keys move one tile at a time and name the direction the
     tile moves:

                hh         slide a tile left
                ll         slide a tile right
                kk         slide a tile up
                jj         slide a tile down
                nn         new game (also the window menu's New entry)

     The status line counts moves - each tile slid counts as one
     - and announces `Solved in N moves!' when the puzzle is
     done; the board then freezes until a new game is dealt.

